{
  "recorded_at_utc": "2026-09-13T05:00:12.8884492Z",
  "status": "0.79.14 OPEN: ordinary Present framepool integrated and host modeled; shared visible statistics and cursor still open.",
  "release": "0.79.13",
  "nvidia": "0.1.97",
  "kernel": "0.1.161",
  "scope": "Actual common queue consumer rotates two/default or three configured private VRAM images sharing one SYSTEM shadow. First-use copies are full; later copies accumulate per-image damage. Full driver-owned source read lease protects the CE region independently of the queue mapping-only reference. A third image can render while a submitted ordinary Window flip holds the other two. No per-frame allocation/table update/selection log after pool setup.",
  "binding": "Real post-init display entry and stall vector, distinct from GSP; actual RM head count and active mode head. No PCI scan, second MSI setup, new kernel/ABI or change to default passive bootfb. Normal GSP-only paths remain intact.",
  "concurrency": "Single gate serializes IRQ service, display enable and retirement. Immutable fields publish before delivery. Per-head atomic seqlock reads have at most three attempts; IRQ updates metadata and signals one existing semaphore. No task-owned lock, BO mutation/free, RM dispatch or log in IRQ. Cached read-only monotonic clock uses existing IRQ-independent kernel clock source where available; it never fabricates an event.",
  "failure": "One CE job, one ready image and one Window flip are bounded by existing deadlines and common depth-one queue. Busy leaves queued work pending; invalid extents finish failed without visibility. Missing FINISHED while the third CE is submitted causes lost/quarantine retaining all image uses and the unacknowledged source read lease. General copy jobs wait for the outstanding flip; mode/catalog/table work cannot enter during Present.",
  "diagnostics": "Existing CE/common queue counters retain device-execution meaning. Per-head Window receipts still separate visible activation and old-image reuse. Selected alias changes at BEGUN/head proof; allocator release follows independent group retirement. Mode diagnostics enumerate up to six shadow aliases and expose pending ready/setup bits 64/128. Shared visible API/statistics are not yet implemented.",
  "validation": {
    "new_gate": false,
    "limits": "Hardware responses and pixels are modeled. No physical output, measured latency, tearing/cursor or performance claim. Existing 51 test groups only; no new guest run. Cursor and shared visible statistics remain unfinished.",
    "checks": {
      "unit-final.log": "13/13 steps succeeded; 51/51 tests passed",
      "build-final.log": "7/7 steps succeeded"
    },
    "device": "Existing actual Device group covers both frame counts, full initialization and several damage rotations with decoded CE pixel comparison; the third image copies while old FINISHED is withheld. Missing FINISHED with CE submitted retains the source lease and all scanout allocations. Common mode apply/confirm/rollback includes candidate frame rotation and complete outgoing-group cleanup. Invalid extents fail once without a read lease or flip. Earlier IRQ/notifier deadline and actual PUT admission checks remain active."
  },
  "open_software": [
    "Hardware cursor plus same visible software fallback integration",
    "Shared per-head/visible Present statistics without reinterpreting copy fences"
  ],
